5977, 0.00916918832808733, 0.00207655131816864, -0.003531247843056917], "index": 15, "object": "embedding"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7567, "total_tokens": 7567}}, "input": {"input": ["# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of July 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's cloud services, highlighting key components, their environments, and recent updates. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud operations around mid-2024.\n\n## SAP Cloud Services Operational Scope\n\nSAP Cloud Services provide a comprehensive suite of cloud-based solutions, including SAP Advanced Financial Closing, Document Management Service, and Forms Service by Adobe. These services operate in various environments, such as Cloud Foundry, Kyma, and Neo, supporting different lines of business, including Finance, Technology, and Intelligent Technologies. Effective management of these services is essential for ensuring the smooth operation of SAP's cloud infrastructure and delivering high-quality services to customers. [Data: Sources (647, 481), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 07), (2024, 07, 09))]\n\n## Document Management Service Updates\n\nThe Document Management Service has undergone several updates, including the deprecation of High Contrast Black and High Contrast White themes, the introduction of the Append Content Stream feature for CMK-enabled repositories, and the availability of the API for restoring capabilities. These updates aim to improve the service's functionality, security, and user experience, ultimately enhancing the overall quality of SAP's cloud services. [Data: Sources (2732, 2733, 2734), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 22), (2024, 07, 09))]\n\n## Forms Service by Adobe Updates\n\nThe Forms Service by Adobe has also received updates, including the availability in additional regions, the introduction of new features, and the update of the Keda module. These updates aim to improve the service's performance, security, and user experience, ultimately enhancing the overall quality of SAP's cloud services. [Data: Sources (2641, 2642, 2643), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 07, 09))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key cloud services, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide innovative solutions and manage technological advancements effectively. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry and SAP Cloud Services\n\nCloud Foundry is a key component of SAP's cloud services, providing a platform for building, deploying, and managing applications. The platform has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of new features and improvements to existing ones. This has enabled SAP to provide innovative solutions to its customers and stay ahead in the market. Effective use of Cloud Foundry has also supported SAP's strategic decision-making processes and ensured continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (647, 720), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 07), (2024, 06, 23))]\n\n## Document Management Service and SAP Cloud Services\n\nThe Document Management Service is a critical component of SAP's cloud services, providing a platform for managing and storing documents. The service has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of new features and improvements to existing ones. This has enabled SAP to provide innovative solutions to its customers and stay ahead in the market. Effective use of the Document Management Service has also supported SAP's strategic decision-making processes and ensured continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. [Data: Sources (2731, 2732), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 07), (2024, 06, 23))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between different departments within SAP, including Risk Management and Legal Compliance, has been instrumental in ensuring that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2734, 2735), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 07), (2024, 06, 23))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technologies, highlighting their core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## Generative AI Hub\n\nThe Generative AI Hub is a key component of SAP's AI strategy, providing a platform for developers to build and deploy AI models. The hub supports various models from different providers, including OpenAI, Meta, and Anthropic. The Generative AI Hub has undergone significant updates in 2024, with new features and models being added regularly. [Data: Sources (2882, 2883, 2884, 2277, 2278), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP AI Core\n\nSAP AI Core is a cloud-based platform that enables developers to build, deploy, and manage AI models. The platform supports various models from different providers, including OpenAI, Meta, and Anthropic. SAP AI Core has undergone significant updates in 2024, with new features and models being added regularly. [Data: Sources (2882, 2883, 2884, 2277), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP AI Launchpad\n\nSAP AI Launchpad is a cloud-based platform that enables developers to build, deploy, and manage AI models. The platform supports various models from different providers, including OpenAI, Meta, and Anthropic. SAP AI Launchpad has undergone significant updates in 2024, with new features and models being added regularly. [Data: Sources (2885, 2886, 2887, 2279), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation\n\nSAP Build Process Automation is a cloud-based platform that enables developers to build, deploy, and manage business processes. The platform has undergone significant updates in 2024, with new features and models being added regularly. [Data: Sources (2271, 2272, 2273, 2274, 2275), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery\n\nSAP Continuous Integration and Delivery is a cloud-based platform that enables developers to build, deploy, and manage business processes. The platform has undergone significant updates in 2024, with new features and models being added regularly. [Data: Sources (2274, 2275, 2276, 2277, 2278), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP Document AI\n\nSAP Document AI is a cloud-based platform that enables developers to build, deploy, and manage AI models. The platform has undergone significant updates in 2024, with new features and models being added regularly. [Data: Sources (2709, 2710), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP Task Center\n\nSAP Task Center is a cloud-based platform that enables developers to build, deploy, and manage business processes. The platform has undergone significant updates in 2024, with new features and models being added regularly. [Data: Sources (2330), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP Print Service\n\nSAP Print Service is a cloud-based platform that enables developers to build, deploy, and manage business processes. The platform has undergone significant updates in 2024, with new features and models being added regularly. [Data: Sources (2392), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 16))]\n\n## SAP Advanced Financial Closing\n\nSAP Advanced Financial Closing is a cloud-based platform that enables developers to build, deploy, and manage business processes. The platform has undergone significant updates in 2024, with new features and models being added regularly. [Data: Sources (2400), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 16))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and maintain regulatory standards. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Logging Improvements\n\nCloud Logging's OpenSearch clusters will be improved by proper index sizing, especially in high-ingest and huge storage volume scenarios. This change will switch from daily indexes to the index rollover approach, targeting the 2501a release (RTC 06.02.25). With this change, the index names will have a new format, without date suffixes, but with a six-digit number suffix. This will further sharpen the retention policy, meaning that the deletion targets indexes created before the last n X 24 hours (where n is the retention configuration) instead of deleting the indexes based on day boundaries (UTC). This also fixes untimely deletion of indexes for customers located further away from UTC. [Data: Sources (1019, 1764), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 17), (2025, 10, 29))]\n\n## Istio Module Updates\n\nThe Istio module has been updated to version 1.22, which enables native sidecars by default. This change resolves network connection issues that arise when regular Istio sidecar proxy containers are not ready at the same time as application containers or init containers. To allow more time for Kyma runtime users to adjust to this change, the Istio module in version 1.21 disables the default use of native sidecars. Although Istio module 1.21 installs Istio updated to version 1.27, by default, Istio sidecar proxies are still deployed as regular sidecar containers. With version 1.22 of the Istio module, Istio proxy sidecars will be deployed by default as native sidecars. [Data: Sources (18), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 05), (2025, 10, 22))]\n\n## SAP BTP Cockpit Updates\n\nSAP BTP introduces new safeguards to prevent accidental force deletion of subaccounts containing content. Global account administrators must now opt in to allow force deletion of subaccounts via a dedicated global account setting. This setting is located under the Subaccounts section in the global account settings and is labeled Enable Subaccounts Force Deletion. For more details on how to access and manage global account settings, see Managing Global Accounts Using the Cockpit (Cloud Foundry) and Managing Global Accounts Using the Cockpit (Neo environment). [Data: Sources (1020), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 04, 17))]", "# Cloud Technology Updates Overview as of 2024-12-12\n\nThis report delves into the key components and updates within the cloud technology framework, highlighting how these entities interact to maintain operational stability and efficiency. The information is relevant to the company's technology operations around mid-2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services component at the company plays a pivotal role in managing and securing user identities. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard the company against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving technology standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3, 4), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## Cloud Logging and Monitoring\n\nThe Cloud Logging component ensures that all company operations adhere to the logging standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on improving the overall stability of Cloud Logging's OpenSearch clusters, noted starting mid-2024, is crucial in maintaining the company's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex logs and monitoring systems. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high logging standards and operational practices. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 01), (2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime component has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of native sidecars and improvements to the API Gateway module. These updates aim to enhance the company's operational efficiency and resilience, ensuring that the company's applications and services remain stable and secure. The updates also reflect the company's commitment to adopting the latest technology standards and best practices. [Data: Sources (6, 7), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 01), (2025, 10, 22))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of December 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, highlighting the components, environments, and improvements made to ensure seamless functionality and compliance. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around December 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Upgrade\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded [Data: Sources (1763), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12))]. This upgrade is crucial for maintaining the security and integrity of SAP's cloud-based services. The upgrade ensures that Cloud Identity Services are up-to-date with the latest security patches and features, providing a robust and reliable identity management solution for SAP's users. Effective identity management is essential for ensuring the security and compliance of SAP's cloud-based services, and this upgrade plays a critical role in achieving this goal. [Data: Sources (1763), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## Cloud Logging Improvements\n\nCloud Logging's OpenSearch clusters will be improved by proper index sizing, especially in high-ingest and huge storage volume scenarios [Data: Sources (1764), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12))]. This improvement will enhance the stability and performance of Cloud Logging, ensuring that users can access their log data efficiently and effectively. The new index naming format will also provide better data retention and deletion policies, reducing the risk of data loss and ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (1764), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## SAP Secure Login Service Update\n\nThe SAP Secure Login Service for SAP GUI has been updated to version 2.10.0 [Data: Sources (1766), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 28))]. This update brings several improvements, including a banner informing about the deprecation of v1beta1 APIRule custom resources and zone-based podAntiAffinity rules for the ory-oathkeeper Deployment. These improvements enhance the security and availability of the SAP Secure Login Service, ensuring that users can access SAP's GUI securely and efficiently. [Data: Sources (1766), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 28))]", "# SAP Technology and Finance Overview as of December 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and finance, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2024.\n\n## SAP Technology Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Technology Department plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (618, 1762), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 12))]\n\n## SAP Finance and Credit Integration\n\nThe SAP Finance Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the financial standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on credit integration, noted starting Q2 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex financial transactions and credit agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high financial standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (1710), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 01), (2024, 12, 19))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Technology and Finance Departments, established in Q2 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are financially sound and that compliance measures consider technological risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with financial compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (1707, 1708), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 01), (2024, 12, 19))]", "# SAP Technology and Financial Management Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and financial management, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Technology Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Technology Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2281, 2285), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## SAP Financial Management and Governance\n\nThe SAP Financial Management Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (1898), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Technology and Financial Management Departments, established in 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2282, 2284), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]", "# Cloud Technology Updates as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and changes in cloud technology, focusing on components such as Kyma Runtime, Decentralized Identity Verification, and Cloud Identity Services. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime has undergone several updates, including the introduction of native sidecars, improved validation for HTTP-based OTLP endpoints, and updates to OTel Collector. These changes aim to enhance the stability and reliability of the reconciliation process for the Istio module's operator. Effective implementation of these updates is crucial for maintaining the company's operational integrity and ensuring compliance with regulatory standards. [Data: Sources (18, 70), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 22), (2025, 10, 29))]\n\n## Decentralized Identity Verification Enhancements\n\nDecentralized Identity Verification has introduced several enhancements, including automated matching of credentials, improvement of the company identity status check, and retrieval of shared verifiable presentation using access tokens. These updates aim to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of the identity verification process, ensuring that the company's operations are secure and compliant with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (322, 323, 324), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 08, 12))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Upgrade\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded, introducing regular upgrades and improved functionality. This update aims to enhance the company's operational stability and ensure compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective implementation of this update is crucial for maintaining the company's operational integrity. [Data: Sources (321), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 12), (2025, 08, 12))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates focusing on various departments and services, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and maintain regulatory standards. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Cloud Logging Service Enhancements\n\nThe Cloud Logging service at SAP has undergone significant enhancements, including the introduction of a dashboard for exploring OpenTelemetry metrics and an OpenTelemetry JVM metrics dashboard. These updates aim to improve the overall stability of Cloud Logging's OpenSearch clusters by proper index sizing, especially in high-ingest and huge storage volume scenarios. The new index format for OpenTelemetry logs and metrics indexes will have a six-digit number suffix instead of the date suffix, allowing for multiple days' data in a single index. This change is scheduled to be rolled out by the end of October 2025. [Data: Sources (14, 16), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 10, 29))]\n\n## Istio Module Updates\n\nThe Istio module at SAP has been updated to version 1.19.3, introducing several improvements, including the fixing of bugs related to label reconciliation and the app.kubernetes.io/version label. The module has also been updated to Istio version 1.26.2. These updates aim to enhance the overall stability and performance of the Istio module. [Data: Sources (17), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 22), (2025, 10, 29))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services at SAP have undergone several updates, including the introduction of new features such as the ability to authenticate a system as administrator using access_token and the ability to configure and assign granular control and access to applications based on custom authorization policies. These updates aim to enhance the overall security and efficiency of the Cloud Identity Services. [Data: Sources (16, 17, 18, 19), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 27), (2025, 10, 29))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes in SAP technology as of 2025, focusing on Variant Configuration, Pricing, and Joule. The information highlights the importance of these updates in enhancing the functionality and usability of SAP systems, particularly in the areas of pricing, configuration, and analytics.\n\n## Variant Configuration Updates\n\nThe Variant Configuration component has seen significant updates, including the addition of new data centers, improved pricing delta replication performance, and enhanced dependency profiling trace capabilities. These changes aim to improve the overall efficiency and accuracy of Variant Configuration, enabling users to make more informed decisions and streamline their workflows. [Data: Sources (29, 30), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 10, 22))]\n\n## Pricing Service Enhancements\n\nThe Pricing Service component has undergone substantial enhancements, including the introduction of new data centers, improved tax calculation capabilities, and enhanced on-request tracing features. These updates aim to improve the accuracy and efficiency of pricing calculations, enabling users to make more informed decisions and reduce errors. [Data: Sources (23, 24, 25, 26, 27), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 10, 22))]\n\n## Joule Updates\n\nJoule has seen significant updates, including the addition of new navigational use cases, enhanced document grounding capabilities, and improved analytical insights features. These changes aim to improve the overall usability and functionality of Joule, enabling users to access and analyze data more efficiently and effectively. [Data: Sources (31, 32, 33, 34, 35, 36, 37, 38), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 02), (2025, 07, 22))]", "# SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing Overview as of October 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates as of October 2025. The information is relevant to the company's operations and technology advancements during this period.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP has undergone significant updates as of October 2025, with new features and enhancements aimed at improving pricing performance and accuracy. These updates include the introduction of dynamic scale base types, validity-based selection of condition records, and US tax calculation via an external engine. These changes are expected to enhance the pricing experience for customers and improve the overall efficiency of the Pricing Service. [Data: Sources (23, 24, 25, 26, 27), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 10, 22))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nThe Pricing Service is now available in the Cloud Foundry environment, providing customers with greater flexibility and scalability. This move is expected to improve the overall user experience and reduce the burden on system administrators. [Data: Sources (23, 24, 25, 26, 27), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 10, 22))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration\n\nCollaboration between the Pricing Service team and other departments, such as Technology and Line of Business, has been instrumental in driving the development and implementation of new features and enhancements. This synergy is vital for ensuring that the Pricing Service meets the evolving needs of customers and the company. [Data: Sources (23, 24, 25, 26, 27), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 10, 22))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and Pricing Service Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components and services of SAP Cloud Foundry and Pricing Service, highlighting their interactions and updates within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Deprecation\n\nThe SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and is going to be removed from SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment. To prevent disruptions and support business continuity, the removal has been postponed to December 31, 2025. Users are recommended to migrate their applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2 as soon as possible. This change affects users who explicitly use the xsenableasyncservice property in their security descriptor and set it to false. [Data: Sources (6), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 08), (2025, 12, 31))]\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service has undergone several updates, including the introduction of new features such as condition supplements in price agreements, dynamic scale base types in price agreements, and validity-based selection of condition records in price agreements. These updates aim to improve the pricing calculation process and ensure accurate handling of time-dependent conditions. [Data: Sources (8, 9, 10, 23, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 10, 22))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment Updates\n\nThe Cloud Foundry environment has been updated to include new features such as the ability to collect traces only for a subset of requests using the ON_REQUEST setting. This update aims to improve the performance and efficiency of the pricing calculation process. [Data: Sources (8, 28), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 10, 22))]", "# SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's Variant Configuration and Pricing key components, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide pricing services and manage variant configurations effectively. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2025.\n\n## Pricing Service Operational Scope\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP plays a pivotal role in providing pricing services and managing variant configurations. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential pricing pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective pricing management not only prevents pricing anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (10, 11, 12), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 19))]\n\n## Variant Configuration and Governance\n\nThe Variant Configuration Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the variant configuration standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on managing variant configurations, noted starting 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex variant configurations and agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high variant configuration standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (13), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 19))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Pricing\n\nCollaboration between the Pricing Service and Variant Configuration Departments, established in 2025, ensures that pricing strategies are legally sound and that variant configuration measures consider pricing risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating pricing management with variant configuration strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (14, 15), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 19))]\n\n## End-of-Life for Synchronous Creation or Update of Service Instances\n\nThe synchronous creation or update of service instances has reached end-of-life. This change affects users who explicitly use the xsenableasyncservice property in their security descriptor and set it to false. To ensure smooth operations, users must adapt their applications to work with asynchronous service instance creation and update before the end-of-life date. [Data: Source (16), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 07), (2026, 01, 19))]\n\n## Update to Cloud Logging's OpenSearch Clusters\n\nThe overall stability of Cloud Logging's OpenSearch clusters will be improved by proper index sizing, especially in high-ingest and huge storage volume scenarios. This change affects users who rely on OpenTelemetry logs and metrics indexes. The new index format will have a six-digit number suffix instead of a date suffix. [Data: Source (17), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 17), (2025, 10, 30))]", "# SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing Overview as of November 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing, highlighting key components, their operational scope, and recent updates. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Pricing Service Operational Scope\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## Variant Configuration and Pricing Updates\n\nRecent updates to Variant Configuration and Pricing, including the introduction of new features such as dependency profiling trace and on-request tracing, demonstrate the company's commitment to improving its services and ensuring compliance with regulatory standards. These updates also highlight the importance of collaboration between different departments and teams within the company. [Data: Sources (3, 4, 5), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime and Telemetry Module\n\nThe Kyma Runtime and Telemetry Module play a crucial role in ensuring the stability and security of SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing's services. The recent update to the Telemetry module, which includes the deletion of the LogParser API, demonstrates the company's commitment to improving its services and ensuring compliance with regulatory standards. [Data: Sources (6, 7), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 01), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## Cloud Logging and OpenSearch Clusters\n\nThe update to Cloud Logging's OpenSearch clusters, which includes the improvement of index sizing, demonstrates the company's commitment to ensuring the stability and security of its services. This update also highlights the importance of collaboration between different departments and teams within the company. [Data: Sources (8, 9), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 11, 12))]\n\n## New Data Center and Regional Availability\n\nThe introduction of a new data center in Microsoft Azure in Australia (Sydney) demonstrates the company's commitment to expanding its services and ensuring compliance with regulatory standards. This update also highlights the importance of collaboration between different departments and teams within the company. [Data: Sources (10, 11), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 01), (2025, 11, 12))]", "# SAP Pricing and Variant Configuration Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's Pricing and Variant Configuration services, highlighting key updates and changes as of 2025. The information is relevant to the company's technology and operations around this time.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP has undergone significant updates, including the support for processing multiple condition records with the same condition type but different validity periods. This feature ensures accurate handling of time-dependent conditions and is crucial for maintaining the integrity of pricing agreements. The update is available as of 2025-11-12 [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 11, 12))].\n\n## US Tax Calculation via External Engine\n\nSAP has introduced support for US tax calculation via an external tax engine, enabling accurate and efficient tax calculations for US taxes. This feature is available as of 2025-11-12 [Data: Sources (3, 4), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 11, 12))].\n\n## Variant Configuration Updates\n\nThe Variant Configuration service at SAP has undergone updates, including the introduction of dependency profiling trace and on-request tracing. These features enable efficient analysis of model performance and collection of traces for a subset of requests. The updates are available as of 2025-11-12 [Data: Sources (5, 6), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 11, 12))].\n\n## Deprecation of LogParser API\n\nThe LogParser API has been deprecated and is scheduled to be deleted by the end of October 2025. Users are required to switch to JSON-based logging instead [Data: Sources (7, 8), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 06), (2025, 10, 30))].\n\n## Cloud Logging Updates\n\nCloud Logging's OpenSearch clusters will be improved by proper index sizing, especially in high-ingest and huge storage volume scenarios. The update is available as of 2025-10-30 [Data: Sources (9, 10), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 17), (2025, 10, 30))]."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_3ce7e25bba7e4d6b54e2ebf8d9a49ac1f4ebbcc65381c7ec319106d6c1e4347e_v2"}